        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " attempt to tie the state legislature’s hands (and voter’s hands) on how Colorado balances its budget and how it can raise revenue for important state priorities. Not content with only the Taxpayer’s Bill of Rights (TABOR) in the Colorado constitution, the measure would put an additional roadblock into raising the income tax for people who make large incomes. Coloradans already have to vote to approve any tax increase.",
